209:{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T12:58:49.490Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"Concrete execution matches CPython on the prompt and edge cases. I also added a structural check: after macro expansion, the readable program term used by the claims is byte-for-byte identical in KORE form to the regenerated `solution.mpy` tree. I’m now adding a small independent contract oracle (score plus strict-best fold) so the proof targets state the contract rather than only hard-coded outputs.","phase":"commentary","memory_citation":null}}
210:{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T12:58:49.490Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0e72b847e9c00506016a60be874c3081908ee7fefff6e1b960","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"Concrete execution matches CPython on the prompt and edge cases. I also added a structural check: after macro expansion, the readable program term used by the claims is byte-for-byte identical in KORE form to the regenerated `solution.mpy` tree. I’m now adding a small independent contract oracle (score plus strict-best fold) so the proof targets state the contract rather than only hard-coded outputs."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f89dd-f7e4-7e91-a8d4-6fc11a5915db"}}}
211:{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T12:58:58.169Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0e72b847e9c00506016a60be8978ec81908893091a08fec7a1","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ltBmOhWMmWWy74gYuP5H1Pkg","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /work/verification.k\\n@@\\n   rule StrongestProgram =>\\n@@\\n         Return(BinOp(\\\"+\\\",\\n           BinOp(\\\"+\\\", Name(\\\"class_name\\\"), Str(\\\".\\\")),\\n           Name(\\\"strongest\\\")))))\\n+\\n+  // A verification-only mathematical rendering of the contract.  It is\\n+  // independent of statement execution: refStrength counts character classes,\\n+  // and refSelect performs a left fold whose strict comparison preserves the\\n+  // first candidate on ties.\\n+  syntax Int ::= \\\"refDelta\\\" \\\"(\\\" String \\\")\\\" [function]\\n+               | \\\"refStrength\\\" \\\"(\\\" String \\\")\\\" [function]\\n+               | \\\"refStrengthAt\\\" \\\"(\\\" String \\\",\\\" Int \\\")\\\" [function]\\n+  syntax String ::= \\\"refStrongest\\\" \\\"(\\\" Values \\\")\\\" [function]\\n+                  | \\\"refSelect\\\" \\\"(\\\" String \\\",\\\" Int \\\",\\\" Values \\\")\\\" [function]\\n+\\n+  rule refDelta(S) => 1\\n+       requires isUpperChar(S)\\n+  rule refDelta(S) => -1\\n+       requires notBool isUpperChar(S) andBool isLowerChar(S)\\n+  rule refDelta(S) => 0\\n+       requires notBool isUpperChar(S) andBool notBool isLowerChar(S)\\n+\\n+  rule refStrength(S) => refStrengthAt(S, 0)\\n+  rule refStrengthAt(S, I) => 0\\n+       requires I >=Int lengthString(S)\\n+  rule refStrengthAt(S, I)\\n+    => refDelta(substrString(S, I, I +Int 1))\\n+       +Int refStrengthAt(S, I +Int 1)\\n+       requires I <Int lengthString(S)\\n+\\n+  rule refStrongest(strVal(S) ; REST)\\n+    => refSelect(S, refStrength(S), REST)\\n+  rule refSelect(BEST, _, .Values) => BEST\\n+  rule refSelect(_, BEST-SCORE, strVal(S) ; REST)\\n+    => refSelect(S, refStrength(S), REST)\\n+       requires refStrength(S) >Int BEST-SCORE\\n+  rule refSelect(BEST, BEST-SCORE, strVal(S) ; REST)\\n+    => refSelect(BEST, BEST-SCORE, REST)\\n+       requires refStrength(S) <=Int BEST-SCORE\\n endmodule\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f89dd-f7e4-7e91-a8d4-6fc11a5915db"}}}
