+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -uo pipefail
+
+scratch=/tmp/audit-work/153-strongest-extension
+spec="$scratch/spec-vacuity-audit.k"
+definition="$scratch/verification-kompiled"
+
+echo '$ kprove spec-vacuity-audit.k --definition verification-kompiled --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY-AUDIT --dry-run'
+kprove "$spec" --definition "$definition" \
+  --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY-AUDIT --dry-run
+build_status=$?
+echo "exit_status=$build_status"
+
+echo '$ kprove spec-vacuity-audit.k --definition verification-kompiled --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY-AUDIT'
+kprove "$spec" --definition "$definition" \
+  --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY-AUDIT
+proof_status=$?
+echo "exit_status=$proof_status (expected nonzero for false returned value)"
+
+if [[ $build_status -ne 0 ]]; then
+  exit 2
+fi
+if [[ $proof_status -eq 0 ]]; then
+  exit 3
+fi
+exit 0

The fresh false-result spec parses/builds successfully and kprove rejects it with the actual correct result in the residual, establishing non-vacuity for the finite claims. Final accounting and report writing remain.
  ✓ Read required Kit skills and verify launcher/provenance integrity
  ✓ Check program fidelity and run independent differential tests
  ✓ Rebuild semantics and proof definitions; execute all positive claims
  ✓ Audit claim adequacy, real-program pinning, and concrete witnesses
  ✓ Inventory and review every semantic/proof rule for soundness
  ✓ Run a fresh false-result non-vacuity mutation
  → Account for proven versus assumed boundaries and write REVIEW.md
